ved_date    removed_case_id  pat gild removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj removed_date    removed_case_id  pat dord removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murj addendum reportaddendum  1 entered  04 04 06  removed_case_id      additional diagnostic information     this report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing additional diagnostic information  the original diagnosis is unchanged  this case has been reviewed by dr  frederick koerner  of the massachusetts general hospital  who concurs with the diagnosis  he comments   i agree wholeheartedly with your analysis of this case  the sections of this core biopsy specimen show a background of slight fibrocystic changes  a population of atypical ductal cells occupies the acini of several terminal duct lobular units in block  1   the cells appear enlarged and they possess slightly enlarged nuclei  homogeneous chromatin  inconspicuous nucleoli  and modest amounts of eosinophilic  apical cytoplasm  the cells grow in a single  crowded layer  they do not show genuine stratification nor do they form cribriform spaces  trabecular bars  or roman bridges  like you  i would classify the proliferation as atypical ductal hyperplasia of columnar cell type  i suspect that the atypical cells represent a neoplastic proliferation  but i cannot exclude the possibility that they constitute an unusual form of ductal hyperplasia  an excision of this region of the patient s left breast would probably clarify this uncertainty  addendum final  ross michael j  m d    removed_date  04 04 06  removed_case_id   by md rosmj edited by  removed_date    removed_case_id  pat murjcodes   removed_accession_id    left breast  no  removed_accession_id    left breast  no atypical  removed_accession_id    columnar epithe  removed_accession_id    columnar epithe lesion  nos  removed_accession_id    columnar epithe atypical hyperp  removed_accession